            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0339" n="309" xml:id="pg309"/>

                <head>125. Letter From the Ambassador at Large (Thompson) to the Assistant Secretary of Defense for
                    International Security Affairs (McNaughton)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d125-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1965-07-17">July 17, 1965</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Dear John:</p>
                <p>The Secretary has carefully considered the points mentioned in Secretary
                        McNamara’s letter of April
                        fifth,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d125-f2"/> regarding the flight of United States
                    helicopters over East Berlin. He has decided that we ought not to resume
                    helicopter flights at this time. In light of his decision, I am sending to you
                    for DOD concurrence a draft joint State-Defense
                    message.2</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">Tommy</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
